+# Chat Interface Skill
+
+## Overview
+
+React-based chat interface with Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming for real-time LLM responses. Supports multi-session management, message actions, foldable thinking panels, and rich markdown rendering with KaTeX for mathematical notation.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Chat interface enables:
+
+- **Real-time streaming**: SSE streaming of LLM responses
+- **Multi-session management**: Multiple chat sessions with search
+- **Message actions**: Copy, edit, regenerate, delete messages
+- **Thinking display**: Foldable panel for LLM reasoning
+- **Rich rendering**: Markdown with KaTeX for LaTeX
+- **Image support**: Display Weibull plots and other images
+- **Export**: Export conversations to Markdown/HTML/PDF
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Component Hierarchy
+
+```
+ChatPage (frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx)
+├── Sidebar (sessions list, search, new chat)
+├── Message List (message items, scrolling)
+│   └── MessageItem (content, actions, thinking)
+├── Composer (input, attachment, send)
+└── SettingsPanel (model config, domain info, theme)
+```
+
+### Service Layer
+
+```
+BackendService (frontend/src/services/types.ts)
+├── streamMessage() - SSE chat streaming
+├── listModels() - Get available models
+├── getLlmConfig() - Get LLM configuration
+├── saveLlmConfig() - Save LLM configuration
+├── testLlmConfig() - Test LLM connection
+├── knowledgeStatus() - Get knowledge base status
+├── uploadDocument() - Upload document to KB
+├── listMcpTools() - List MCP tools
+└── downloadFile() - Download static files
+```
+
+## SSE Streaming
+
+### Stream Events
+
+The backend streams events via SSE:
+
+```typescript
+type ChatStreamEvent =
+  | { type: 'token'; text: string }           // Text token
+  | { type: 'thought'; text: string }         // Thinking/reasoning
+  | { type: 'tool_start'; name: string }      // Tool invocation start
+  | { type: 'tool_end'; name: string }        // Tool invocation end
+  | { type: 'image'; url: string }            // Plot image URL
+  | { type: 'done'; content: string; image_url: string | null }  // Completion
+  | { type: 'error'; message: string };       // Error
+```
+
+### Streaming Implementation
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/services/http.ts`
+
+```typescript
+export async function streamSse(
+  baseUrl: string,
+  path: string,
+  body: object,
+  onEvent: (event: ChatStreamEvent) => void,
+  signal?: AbortSignal
+): Promise<void> {
+  const response = await fetch(resolveBackendUrl(baseUrl, path), {
+    method: 'POST',
+    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
+    body: JSON.stringify(body),
+    signal,
+  });
+
+  const reader = response.body!.getReader();
+  const decoder = new TextDecoder();
+
+  while (true) {
+    const { done, value } = await reader.read();
+    if (done) break;
+
+    const chunk = decoder.decode(value);
+    const lines = chunk.split('\n');
+
+    for (const line of lines) {
+      if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {
+        const data = JSON.parse(line.slice(6));
+        onEvent(data);
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Thinking Splitter
+
+The frontend classifies streamed tokens as thinking vs answer:
+
+**File**: `backend/src/host/app.py` (backend-side)
+
+```python
+class StreamThoughtSplitter:
+    """Classify streamed tokens as thinking vs answer without waiting for full reply."""
+    def feed(self, delta: str) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:
+        # Returns [('thought', text)] or [('token', text)]
+```
+
+## Message Management
+
+### Session Storage
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/hooks/useSessions.ts`
+
+```typescript
+export function useSessions(storage: Storage) {
+  const [sessions, setSessions] = useState<ChatSession[]>([]);
+  const [currentId, setCurrentId] = useState<string>('');
+  const [messages, setMessages] = useState<Message[]>([]);
+
+  // Load from localStorage on mount
+  // Save to localStorage on change
+  // New chat, select session, delete session, clear all
+}
+```
+
+### Message Structure
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/types/chat.ts`
+
+```typescript
+export interface Message {
+  id: string;
+  role: 'user' | 'assistant';
+  content: string;
+  timestamp: number;
+  model?: string;
+  stats?: string;              // "12.3s · ~328 tokens"
+  imageUrl?: string;          // Plot image URL
+  thinkingText?: string;      // Thinking content
+  thinkingSteps?: string[];   // Individual thinking steps
+  thinkingOpen?: boolean;     // Foldable state
+  thinkingMs?: number;        // Thinking duration
+}
+```
+
+### Session Structure
+
+```typescript
+export interface ChatSession {
+  id: string;
+  title: string;
+  messages: Message[];
+  updatedAt: number;
+}
+```
+
+## Rich Rendering
+
+### Markdown Rendering
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx`
+
+```typescript
+<ReactMarkdown
+  remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}
+  rehypePlugins={[rehypeSanitize]}
+  components={{
+    // Custom components for code blocks, tables, etc.
+  }}
+>
+  {content}
+</ReactMarkdown>
+```
+
+**Features**:
+- GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM)
+- HTML sanitization (security)
+- Code blocks with syntax highlighting
+- Tables
+- Task lists
+- Strikethrough
+
+### KaTeX Integration
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/components/MessageItem.tsx`
+
+```tsx
+<ReactMarkdown
+  remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm, remarkMath]}
+  rehypePlugins={[
+    [rehypeSanitize, katexSanitizeSchema],
+    [rehypeKatex, { output: 'html', throwOnError: false, strict: false }],
+  ]}
+>
+  {content}
+</ReactMarkdown>
+```
+
+**Rendering rules**:
+- Declarative KaTeX (`remark-math` + `rehype-katex`), not MathJax typesetting.
+- Sanitize runs **before** KaTeX: KaTeX HTML positions sub/superscripts and
+  fractions with inline styles, which a later sanitize pass would strip and
+  collapse (e.g. `$B_{10}$` stacking its `10` below the `B`). Raw-HTML styles
+  from the message source are still neutralized by the sanitize pass.
+- Standard LaTeX notation: `$B_{10}$`, `$\beta$`, `$\eta$` (legacy `\sb{}`
+  still maps to a subscript for old messages; new output must not use it).
+
+### Math Repair
+
+**Files**: `frontend/src/utils/mathMarkdown.ts`, `backend/src/common/markdown_math.py`
+(mirrored logic — keep both in sync)
+
+```typescript
+export function patchMarkdownMath(text: string): string {
+  // Normalize math delimiters to $...$ / $$...$$, balance braces,
+  // escape bare %, and move [source] citations out of math delimiters.
+}
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Repair common LLM TeX mistakes (unclosed delimiters, unbalanced
+braces, citations glued inside `$...$`) before Markdown/KaTeX rendering, so
+formulas render instead of breaking.
+
+## Message Actions
+
+### Copy
+
+**Implementation**: Clipboard API
+
+```typescript
+navigator.clipboard.writeText(content);
+```
+
+### Edit and Resend
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User clicks edit on message
+2. Message content loaded into composer
+3. User modifies and sends
+3. Original message replaced with new message
+4. LLM regenerates response
+
+### Regenerate
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User clicks regenerate on assistant message
+2. Last user message resent to LLM
+3. New response generated
+4. Old assistant message replaced
+
+### Delete
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User clicks delete on message
+2. Message removed from session
+3. If session empty, session deleted
+
+## Image Rendering
+
+### Plot Images
+
+**Flow**:
+1. Backend generates plot (e.g., `weibull_abc123.png`)
+2. Backend returns `image` event with URL
+3. Frontend displays image in message
+4. Image served from `/static/` directory
+
+**Implementation**:
+```typescript
+{imageUrl && (
+  <img
+    src={resolveStaticUrl(imageUrl)}
+    alt="Generated plot"
+    className="message-image"
+  />
+)}
+```
+
+## Export Functionality
+
+### Export Formats
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx`
+
+**Formats**:
+- **Markdown**: Plain markdown export
+- **HTML**: Rendered HTML export
+- **PDF**: Browser print to PDF
+
+**Implementation**:
+```typescript
+const handleExport = async (format: ExportFormat) => {
+  if (format === 'markdown') {
+    // Export as markdown
+  } else if (format === 'html') {
+    // Export as HTML
+  } else if (format === 'pdf') {
+    // Print to PDF via browser
+  }
+};
+```
+
+## Settings Panel
+
+### LLM Configuration
+
+**Fields**:
+- Provider (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp, OpenAI, custom)
+- Base URL
+- API key (write-only, not persisted in localStorage)
+- Model selection
+- Temperature
+- System prompt
+
+**API**:
+- `GET /api/llm/config` - Get current config
+- `PUT /api/llm/config` - Save config
+- `POST /api/llm/test` - Test connection
+
+### MCP Tool Inventory
+
+**API**:
+- `GET /api/mcp/tools` - List MCP tools
+
+**Display**:
+- Tool list in Settings
+
+### Knowledge Base Status
+
+**API**:
+- `GET /api/knowledge/status` - Get KB status
+
+**Display**:
+- Embedding model
+- File count
+- Chunk count
+- Indexed files
+
+## Theme Support
+
+### Theme Options
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/hooks/useTheme.ts`
+
+**Options**:
+- **System**: Follow OS light/dark setting
+- **Light**: Always light theme
+- **Dark**: Always dark theme
+
+**Implementation**:
+```typescript
+const [choice, setChoice] = useState<ThemeChoice>('system');
+
+useEffect(() => {
+  const prefersDark = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
+  const isDark = choice === 'dark' || (choice === 'system' && prefersDark);
+  document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-bs-theme', isDark ? 'dark' : 'light');
+}, [choice]);
+```
+
+### CSS Variables
+
+**File**: `frontend/src/styles.css`
+
+```css
+:root {
+  --bg-primary: #ffffff;
+  --text-primary: #212529;
+}
+
+[data-bs-theme="dark"] {
+  --bg-primary: #212529;
+  --text-primary: #f8f9fa;
+}
+```
+
+## Performance Characteristics
+
+### Streaming Performance
+
+- **First token**: < 500ms (LLM latency)
+- **Token rate**: 10-50 tokens/second (depends on LLM)
+- **UI responsiveness**: Smooth with 60fps rendering
+- **Memory**: Linear with message count
+
+### Rendering Performance
+
+- **Markdown rendering**: < 100ms per message
+- **MathJax rendering**: < 200ms per message
+- **Image loading**: < 500ms (depends on image size)
+
+## Best Practices
+
+### Streaming
+
+1. **Use SSE**: Prefer SSE over polling for real-time updates
+2. **Handle errors**: Display error messages to user
+3. **Support cancellation**: Use AbortSignal for cancellation
+4. **Buffer display**: Don't render every token immediately (buffer small bursts)
+
+### Message Management
+
+1. **Limit history**: Don't keep unlimited session history
+2. **Use localStorage**: Persist sessions for continuity
+3. **Auto-save**: Save on every message
+4. **Search**: Enable session search for navigation
+
+### Rendering
+
+1. **Sanitize HTML**: Use rehype-sanitize for security
+2. **Lazy load images**: Load images as they appear
+3. **Debounce MathJax**: Don't render on every token
+4. **Use virtual scrolling**: For very long conversations
+
+## Related Skills
+
+- **Model Picker**: LLM provider and model selection
+- **Settings Panel**: Configuration interface
+
+## References
+
+- React 19 Documentation: https://react.dev/
+- React Bootstrap: https://react-bootstrap.github.io/
+- React Markdown: https://github.com/remarkjs/react-markdown
+- MathJax: https://www.mathjax.org/
