+## API Key Security
+
+### Write-Only API Key
+
+**Design**: API key is never persisted in localStorage/sessionStorage
+
+**Flow**:
+1. User enters API key in settings
+2. Key stored in React memory only
+3. Key sent to backend via `PUT /api/llm/config`
+4. Backend encrypts and stores key in `backend/.llm_secret.enc`
+5. Key never returned by GET endpoints
+6. Key not saved in browser storage
+
+**Backend Storage**:
+**File**: `backend/src/common/credential_store.py`
+
+```python
+def set_api_key(user: str, key: str) -> None:
+    """Encrypt and store API key."""
+    encrypted = fernet.encrypt(key.encode())
+    secret_path.write_bytes(encrypted)
+    _chmod_owner_only(secret_path)
+```
+
+### Per-User Keys
+
+**Multi-User Mode**:
+- Keys namespaced per user ID
+- User ID hashed before use
+- Each user has separate encrypted key file
+
